#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:190
msgid ""
"Set `bundled: false` to switch all five off at once; `disabled` turns off "
"only the ones you name and is ignored when `bundled` is false. An "
"unrecognized name is warned about in the server log and otherwise ignored, "
"so a typo here never takes the other wordlists down with it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:195
msgid ""
"See `rust-core/dictionaries/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md` for each list's source "
"and licensing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:198
msgid "Hyphenated words"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:200
msgid ""
"A hyphenated compound is accepted when every one of its parts is known "
"individually, so `Chern-Simons` resolves from `chern` and `simons`. This "
"matters because engines disagree about what they report: Harper flags the "
"parts of a compound separately, while LanguageTool flags the whole span. "
"Requiring *all* parts to be known keeps genuine typos visible — `Chern-"
"Simmmons` and `well-knownn` are still reported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:207
msgid ""
"The same rule applies to words you add yourself and to any file listed in "
"`paths`, not just the bundled wordlists."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:210
msgid "Your own words"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:212
msgid ""
"*Add to dictionary* in the editor writes to `.languagecheck/dictionary.txt` "
"in the workspace. That file is yours; the bundled wordlists are never "
"written back to it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:215
msgid "Morphology"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:217
msgid ""
"One dictionary entry covers the words built on it. Adding `algebra` also "
"accepts `algebras`, `subalgebra`, `sub-algebra` and `algebraicity`, so the "
"dictionary stops growing one line per inflection. On by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:59
msgid "Accept a flagged word that decomposes into a known root"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:59
msgid "`inflections`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:59
msgid "Also accept the regular inflections of dictionary words"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:232
msgid ""
"Two switches because the two halves work differently, and can fail "
"differently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:235
msgid "Prefixes and derivational suffixes are recognized"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:237
msgid ""
"A word that is flagged as a misspelling is re-read as a productive prefix "
"(`sub-`, `semi-`, `non-`, `quasi-`, `counter-`, … — the full list is in "
"`rust-core/dictionaries/affixes/prefixes.txt`) and/or a derivational suffix "
"(`-ness`, `-ity`, `-able`, `-ly`, …) over a root. The root has to be a real "
"word — one of yours, one from a bundled list, or one Harper knows — so "
"`subalgebra` is accepted and `subxyzzy` is not. The closed and hyphenated "
"spellings take the same path, because Harper and LanguageTool disagree about "
"which one they report."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:246
msgid ""
"This is done by taking the word apart rather than by listing the results, "
"because prefixes stack freely: the set of words `algebra` licenses is "
"unbounded, so there is nothing to list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:250
msgid "Inflections are generated"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:252
msgid ""
"Plurals, and the past and progressive of `-ate`/`-ize`/`-ise`/`-ify` verbs, "
"are generated from each dictionary word when the workspace loads and then "
"matched like any other entry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:256
msgid ""
"Generated, not stripped, because the spelling rules only run one way. "
"`occur` plus `-ed` is `occurred`; a checker that instead removed `-ed` from "
"`occured` would find `occur` and accept a misspelling. The same shape "
"accepts `childs` and `mouses`, which is why plurals are never recognized by "
"taking a word apart."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:261
msgid "What keeps typos visible"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:263
msgid ""
"A decomposition on its own is weak evidence: `untill` reads as `un-` + "
"`till`, and `till` really is a word. So the engine's own correction has the "
"final say — if it can offer something one edit away from what you typed, the "
"squiggle stays. A word with no plausible correction is what a genuine "
"coinage looks like."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:268
msgid "Names"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:270
msgid ""
"Opt-in suppression of spelling diagnostics on human names. Off by default."
msgstr ""

